notesT: Two camera-pulse fixes from your device logs — the pulse should now lock AND hold.
  FIX 1 (weak-signal): if the red level drifted across the finger-detection threshold, the
  app used to flip "finger yes/no", wiping the heart-rate estimate each time so it never
  locked. Finger detection now has hysteresis — once detected it HOLDS through dips.
  FIX 2 (strong-signal): once locked (nice steady BPM), a tiny finger-pressure change made
  the amplitude briefly spike, which tripped the motion filter and WIPED the whole lock in
  one instant — even though your pulse was still perfectly readable. Now, when the pulse is
  clearly there, a brief movement barely dents the lock instead of resetting it.
  Test 10.79.3: Bio page → cover the rear camera + flash, hold ~15–20 s → BPM should lock
  AND stay locked through small movements (confidence holds, not flickering to "—").
  Known next item if it still shows: a rare too-bright exposure lock → brief "re-settle".
  Also carries 10.79.1's polish (Breathing only on Bio, ≥44pt taps, consistent theme).
